  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: The largest gain so far comes from switching to multi-profile with scVI_n200 (0.520→0.650, +13 pts), while PCA_n2000 single-profile scores 0.485 and scGPT single-profile scores 0.411. Aggregation (avgpool vs transformer) shows negligible difference with scVI. Uncertainty: It is unclear whether the multi-profile gain is a general property of having more biological profiles (i.e., more information per cell) or is specific to scVI's learned latent representation. This experiment (PCA_n2000, multi-profile, avgpool) fills in the encoder×profile 2×2 grid: if PCA also jumps substantially, the gain is profile-driven and any encoder benefits; if PCA shows little improvement, the gain is representation-specific to scVI. This cleanly isolates one variable (encoder) against the already-established multi-profile setting, making it the most informative single experiment under budget constraints before committing to multimodal or alternative encoders."
}

